  "comment": "About 160 species of south Louisiana: the 150 bird species with the most research-grade iNaturalist observations created up to 2026-11-09 across 26 parishes from Lake Pontchartrain's north shore to the Texas line (Greater New Orleans, the river parishes, Baton Rouge, the Atchafalaya, Acadiana, Lake Charles and the coast from Plaquemines to Cameron), minus the domestic Greylag Goose, plus ten heard more than seen or missed by the ranking (King Rail, Sora, Marsh Wren, Eastern Screech Owl, Chuck-will's-widow, Acadian Flycatcher, Swainson's and Kentucky Warblers, Seaside Sparrow, Mottled Duck). Feral Muscovy Ducks and Mute Swans stay in: they are what one meets in the city parks. `packbuilder draft --place 2109 --place 2126 --place 107079 --place 966 --place 107084 --place 107088 --place 107085 --place 107083 --place 1989 --place 1004 --place 2108 --place 1642 --place 1984 --place 2208 --place 1643 --place 124 --place 2098 --place 107087 --place 107080 --place 1048 --place 125 --place 1620 --place 1045 --place 1986 --place 1831 --place 1832 --before 2026-11-09 --top 150 --exclude 'Anser anser' --add ...`. scientific_name and common_name follow the BirdNET+ label file as in us-ca-la (species the committed packs already list reuse their entries); inat_taxon_id is iNaturalist's; wikipedia_url is iNaturalist's link for the taxon. The order is the observation ranking, then the species added by hand. Drafted with `packbuilder draft` and read over by a person; tests/test_definition.py checks the labels.",
